# Review ownership.
#
# GitHub cannot stop a pull request being opened, so this does not prevent one. What it does
# is guarantee that anything touching these paths cannot merge without an explicit review —
# which matters most for the paths where an automated check is not the safety net.

# Everything, by default.
*                       @PatMacalister

# The landing page is not open to contributions. It is published marketing copy for a tool
# whose credibility depends on not overclaiming, and its wording is deliberate — "never
# alarmist, never overclaim coverage, consequence language". Copy changes from outside are
# declined; see CONTRIBUTING.md. Bug reports about the page are welcome as issues.
/public/                @PatMacalister

# The egress allowlist and the module contract are the two places where review is the only
# real control. apiHosts is checked for shape, never for legitimacy: only a human can tell
# whether a hostname is genuinely the provider's API. Provider modules also execute at import,
# before validation, so the whole file has to be read — not just the diff.
